#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:1
msgid "Security Policies and Procedures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:3
msgid "Reporting a Bug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:5
msgid ""
"The `cookie` team and community take all security bugs seriously. Thank "
"you for improving the security of the project. We appreciate your efforts"
" and responsible disclosure and will make every effort to acknowledge "
"your contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:10
msgid ""
"Report security bugs by emailing the current owner(s) of `cookie`. This "
"information can be found in the npm registry using the command `npm owner"
" ls cookie`. If unsure or unable to get the information from the above, "
"open an issue in the [project issue "
"tracker](https://github.com/jshttp/cookie/issues) asking for the current "
"contact information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:17
msgid ""
"To ensure the timely response to your report, please ensure that the "
"entirety of the report is contained within the email body and not solely "
"behind a web link or an attachment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/cookie_SECURITY.md:21
msgid ""
"At least one owner will acknowledge your email within 48 hours, and will "
"send a more detailed response within 48 hours indicating the next steps "
"in handling your report. After the initial reply to your report, the "
"owners will endeavor to keep you informed of the progress towards a fix "
"and full announcement, and may ask for additional information or "
"guidance."
msgstr ""

